### Agent memory: read the map, then the area

Claude Code loads only the head of your memory index, `MEMORY.md`, at
session start (at most 200 lines / 25,000 bytes), and the shared index is
budgeted for it whichever harness you run. When an `areas/` directory sits beside it,
the index is split and `MEMORY.md` is a map: one line per area, each saying
when to read `areas/<slug>.md`. **Before you start work, open the area index
whose hook matches your task** — that is where the lessons for it are. File a
new memory's pointer in its area index (link `../<file>.md`), or set
`metadata.area: <slug>` in its frontmatter; `work memory persist` reports the
index size against the limit and files stray map entries for you.
